  "claim": "Sir William James Ingram, 1st Baronet (27 October 1847 – 18 December 1924) was Managing Director of \"The Illustrated London News\", which appeared first on Saturday 14 May 1842, as the world's first illustrated weekly news magazine, and appeared weekly until summer 1971.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Sir William Ingram, 1st Baronet. Sentence: Sir William James Ingram, 1st Baronet (27 October 1847 – 18 December 1924) was Managing Director of \"The Illustrated London News\" and a Liberal politician who sat in the House of Commons in three periods between 1878 and 1895.\nPage: The Illustrated London News. Sentence: Founded by Herbert Ingram, it appeared weekly until 1971, then less frequently thereafter, and ceased publication in 2003.",
